<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS UNLEADED GASOLINES PRICES.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS UNLEADED GASOLINES PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland said on Thursday it will cut its retail prices for most of its unleaded and lead-substituted gasolines in the Netherlands by one cent per litre from September 23.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, it said.</p>
<p>The price of lead-substituted super will go down to 2,12 guilders from 2,13 per litre. The price of unleaded Euro falls to 2,00 from 2,01 and unleaded super will go down to 2,05 from 2,06 guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
